1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:08,600
Three small laws — idempotence, projection, and lambdas without bounds checks. Every layer that follows is a composition of them, and nothing more.

2
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:17,600
Join: a product with two properties and nothing else. "a j b" is the one constructor the whole system needs.

3
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:27,600
Series: a length joined to a lambda. Reading index i calls the function — the size travels as data beside it, so the hot path carries no array and no bounds check.

4
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:37,600
Projection: α maps without materializing. Chains of α fuse into one lambda, and index views — s[ix], s[range] — project the domain instead of copying the data.

5
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:47,600
Idempotence: asking twice is free. Meta suppliers, decoded leaves, revisions and replays can all be re-run without changing the answer — so any lambda may be called anywhere, at any time.

6
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:57,600
Cursor: a Series of rows, each row a Series of value ⋈ meta. A table is three Joins and two lambdas deep — and the child slot lets any cell be a whole document.

7
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:07,600
ISAM Cursors: fixed-width records on memory-mapped files. The row lambda becomes an offset computation — the same Cursor algebra, now zero-copy over disk.

8
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:18,600
Confix: one parser for JSON, YAML and CBOR. Its index is faceted — spans, tags, depths, children — and the parse geometry is itself an ISAM Cursor. Document ⇄ table is an isomorphism, not an import.

9
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:28,600
The fortress: a Couch over Confix documents, a write-ahead log and a copy-on-write B+tree. Its wire speaks CouchDB — and every block is also a content address.

10
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:39,600
CCEK reactors on every side: each service is a CoroutineContext Element found by its Key. No god object — the coroutine context is the registry, and every reactor runs as its own SupervisorJob.

11
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:51,600
Transparency: SQL, PostgREST, facet search and graph walks are not separate databases. They are projections of the same Cursor — one AST, one planner, the same column kernels.

12
00:01:52,400 --> 00:02:01,600
Unified I/O: io_uring shot through every layer. ISAM pages, the userspace Btrfs volume and the network transport submit through one liburing seam; completions arrive as values the lambdas above simply read.

13
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:12,600
Agents on a blackboard, in concentric networks. Models only propose; the Rete agenda decides; every conclusion links back to the sentence it came from.

14
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:23,600
Ouroboros: the system’s own code, worktree and history become content-addressed blocks — replicated peer to peer over IPNS, and hot-swapped into the running daemon.

15
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:33,600
And the payoff: AI models served from this fabric. Weights are content-addressed blocks, requests are reactor events, output is a stream — and the latest master is ready to release.

16
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:44,600
Compositional density: each layer is the layer below joined with a lambda. Idempotence makes it safe, projection makes it free, and lambdas without bounds checks keep it fast.
